                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The OG Fallout, with a lot of content, a lot of voice acting, some very nice musical moments (though the first one is the best).   There's a rather impressive ending song that changes depending on your choices.  That kind of thing really sticks with me.  No mods strictly necessary for a good playthrough (as opposed to my 200 odd for New Vegas or the 40,000 that are necessary to make FO4 have a good plot.)\n\nIt's a solid RPG, in a lot of ways, which while not breaking the mold entirely, does make you interested in the world without the usual holes that develop in games that try to do too much.\n\nThe top review is about bugs... I never encountered these ones.  There are some irritating ones, and a few UI issues once in a while.  Nothing is horrendous.\n\nI would however recommend that if you want a particular ending on your second run-through, like the rather tricky November Reigns ending, that you use the online save game editor.\n\nLastly, this is one of the very few games that make me say to myself \"Yeah, if I never play another video game, I'll be fine.  I'm glad this was the last one.\"  Make of that what you will.",
